# .trivyignore — CVE allowlist for the CI Trivy gate (ISI-6865, Phase 4 of ISI-6741).
#
# HOW THE GATE WORKS (.github/workflows/ci.yml → "Trivy CVE gate" step on each service):
#   trivy image --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed --exit-code 1
#   with --trivyignores .trivyignore
# The gate FAILS a PR when a build introduces a NEW *fixable* CRITICAL/HIGH that is not
# listed below. The two filters that keep it from red-failing on the accepted baseline:
#   1. --ignore-unfixed  → the upstream-unfixed tail (no FixedVersion) never gates. This is
#      exactly the ISI-6778 carry rule ("carried iff no FixedVersion"), so the 15 CVEs in the
#      ISI-6778 registry are auto-excluded and need no entry here (listed at the bottom for ref).
#   2. this allowlist    → the fixable CRITICAL/HIGH already present on the v0.0.14 images at
#      baseline time. These ARE actionable; they are accepted *temporarily* and tracked for
#      burn-down in the Phase 5 follow-up. Each carries an expires: date so a suppression is
#      never a silent perpetual mute — re-justify or (better) remove it by bumping the dep.
#
# CONVENTION: the comment line directly above each CVE id carries
#   <CVE-ID>  severity:  pkg:  fixed:  svc:  expires:YYYY-MM-DD  justification:<why accepted>
# KEEP IN SYNC: regenerate after any base/dep bump or re-scan (recipe in ISI-6865 thread).
#   Source of truth for the upstream-unfixed tail: ISI-6778 carried-CVE registry.
#
# Format ref: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# ===================================================================================
# BASELINE — fixable CRITICAL/HIGH present on v0.0.14 images (vuln DB 2026-10-29).
# Original baseline: 65 distinct CVEs (2 CRITICAL / 63 HIGH). Phase 5 (ISI-6867) burn-down COMPLETE.
# BURN-DOWN LOG:
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6867): product-catalog + load-generator-dynatrace Go builders bumped
#     golang:1.25-alpine -> golang:1.26.10-alpine. Cleared 22 stdlib CVEs (toolchain was
#     1.26.0 via GOTOOLCHAIN=auto; 1.26.10 fixes all stdlib advisories ≤1.26.10). -> 43 remain.
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6881, PR#40): load-generator + load-generator-dynatrace xk6 Go deps pinned
#     (grpc 1.83.2, x/net 0.60.0, klauspost 1.18.7; x/crypto/x/text/otel resolve safe via MVS)
#     and toolchain forced to go1.26.10. Cleared ~23 load-gen CVEs incl. CRITICAL CVE-2026-33186.
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6885, PR#36): grpc_health_probe v0.4.60 -> v0.4.61 (go-jose/v4 4.1.6).
#     Cleared CVE-2026-116587 (go-jose/v4).
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6883, PR#39): cart base 24 -> 25-jre-alpine + guava constraint 33.7.2-jre.
#     Cleared CVE-2026-111497 (brotli-libs, CRITICAL) + CVE-2026-102554 (guava).
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6882, PR#38): frontend npm transitive deps cleared by node:25-alpine +
#     next16/react19 lockfile regen. Removed the 9 frontend suppressions.
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6884, PR#37): checkout pip floor pins msgpack==1.2.3 / urllib3==2.8.0 /
#     setuptools==84.2.1 force the CVE-fixed transitive versions into the image.
#   2026-10-30 (ISI-6867 reconcile): removed the final 9 now-stale suppressions —
#     * 5 checkout (CVE-2025-47273, CVE-2026-114613, CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97689,
#       GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964): the ISI-6884 pins landed on main but the matching allowlist
#       cleanup was dropped in a rebase; the CVEs are already fixed in the built image.
#     * 4 product-catalog x/net+stdlib (CVE-2026-33814 / 39821 / 46600 / 78669): both sides now
#       fixed — go.mod carries golang.org/x/net v0.62.0 (>= 0.60.0) and the builder is
#       golang:1.26.10-alpine (stdlib >= 1.26.9). Verified clean by the per-service CI Trivy gate.
# Remaining fixable baseline: 0 (0 CRITICAL / 0 HIGH). The active allowlist below is EMPTY;
# the only suppressed CVEs are the ISI-6778 upstream-unfixed tail (reference section), which
# carry no FixedVersion and are auto-excluded by the gate's --ignore-unfixed.
# ===================================================================================

# ===================================================================================
# REFERENCE ONLY — ISI-6778 carried upstream-unfixed tail (15 distinct HIGH, 0 CRIT).
# These have NO upstream FixedVersion and are already excluded by --ignore-unfixed, so they
# need no active entry. Listed here so this file stays legible against the ISI-6778 registry.
# Exit condition: upstream vendor ships a fix (Debian trixie / go-jose / http-cache-semantics
# / otel-contrib) → the CVE flips to fixable and the gate surfaces it for remediation.
#   CVE-2026-76642 CVE-2026-78408 CVE-2026-78409 CVE-2026-78410  (util-linux src, trixie)
#   CVE-2025-69720 (ncurses)  CVE-2026-16742 (systemd)  CVE-2026-54369 (libacl1)
#   CVE-2026-58471 CVE-2026-58472 (wget)  CVE-2026-9538 (perl-base, Debian fix_deferred)
#   CVE-2026-116587 (go-jose/v3 — upstream-unfixed; the go-jose/v4 variant was fixable and is remediated via ISI-6885, grpc_health_probe v0.4.61)
#   CVE-2026-41567 CVE-2026-42306 CVE-2026-42602 (collector: docker/docker, azureauthext)
#   CVE-2026-93748 (frontend: http-cache-semantics)
# ===================================================================================
